Arcade bar: a NAOMI game's BIOS from its own ROM set.

loadMameRom loaded the BIOS with the ROM set's file name only (settings.content.fileName,
"vtennisg.zip"), which naomi_cart_LoadBios opens as an archive relative to the working directory:
that fails, and the BIOS EPROMs inside the set are never seen, so a separate naomi.zip in
<system>/dc was required. MAME's sets merged with their BIOS (the bar's vtennisg.zip) carry the
EPROMs themselves: open the set by its full path (Emulator::loadGame's second BIOS load already
does), and the BIOS is found by CRC in it, as loadBios intends.

diff --git a/core/hw/naomi/naomi_cart.cpp b/core/hw/naomi/naomi_cart.cpp
--- a/core/hw/naomi/naomi_cart.cpp
+++ b/core/hw/naomi/naomi_cart.cpp
@@ -265,7 +265,10 @@
 	}
 
 	// Load the BIOS
-	naomi_cart_LoadBios(fileName.c_str());
+	// Arcade bar (flycast/patches/0004): by the ROM set's full path, so its own copy of the BIOS
+	// is found (the file name alone is opened relative to the working directory, which fails, and
+	// only a separate <system>/dc/naomi.zip would do).
+	naomi_cart_LoadBios(path.c_str());
 
 	// Now load the cartridge data
 	try {
